 "notes": [
  "Positions only: every byte comes from the user's own ROM set at extraction time.",
  "Tile sheets are 8-bit indexed PNGs in color: the 16 palettes the sheet's tiles are shown with the most (tile_palettes.json, positions in the program ROM), a tile's pixels at its palette's slot * 16 + pen, so index & 15 is the pen; pen 0 is transparent. Each sheet's JSON says every tile's palette. 32 sheets of 1024 tiles: the tile ROM's 32768.",
  "MultiPCM samples (the pcm region, 4 MB): the 512 sample headers at its start as text (pcm_headers.txt), then the region as 8-bit WAVs, one byte a WAV sample: common.wav, the rest of the first MB, which the chip always reads; and bank_2.wav to bank_7.wav, the 512 KB pages the sound sets put in the chip's two windows (screen 1's at 100000, screen 2's at 180000; its headers are 100 on). Each WAV's JSON lists the samples the headers start in it and the sound sets that use the page. The rate is nominal.",
  "Sprites: every piece record (0x122B74, 12 bytes each: a piece's size and place in the sprite ROM) in sprite sheets (sprite_sheets.txt: a family's or a stretch of animations' sheet, a row per animation): indexed PNGs with the palettes the pieces are drawn with (sprite_palettes.json: positions in the program ROM, and which records are 8 bits a pen or drawn opaque), and a JSON beside each that says where each piece is in the sheet and where it goes back in the sprite ROM; what no record covers as strips in unused/. Pen 0 is transparent.",
  "Program data (the program ROM, 2 MB: the code chips at 000000, which the board repeats four times, and the data chips at 100000): text files, a section a piece, cut where symbols.txt names a place and where the C reads a table (src/ram.h), in the format data_formats.json gives it (16-bit words or bytes in hex if none), grouped by subject where data_formats.json says, else by the 64 KB they are in; the code and the mirrors are left out (the C replaces the code). layout.json lists the pieces in order.",
  "Sound program (epr-15550, 512 KB): its data as text files the same way, cut where sound_symbols.txt names a place (sound_formats.json, else by the 8 KB bank they are in); its code is left out (the C replaces it), its jump tables are data (the driver reads them before it jumps)."
 ],
